    a = lambda k, c='analysis_759': t1[k][c]
    p(f"Of 2,596 second-examination records, 1,859 were MEC examinations; 979 participants were eligible and {pr['n']} had complete inputs at both visits (Figure 1). Their mean age was {F(a('age')['mean'])} years, {F(a('female')['pct'])}% were women, and the median first-visit PREVENT-ASCVD risk was {F(a('risk')['median'], 2)}% (IQR, {F(a('risk')['q1'], 2)}–{F(a('risk')['q3'], 2)}%; Table 1). Compared with the weighted eligible NHANES III population, participants were older, more often Black or Mexican American and more often had diabetes, and their median risk was higher ({F(a('risk')['median'], 2)}% vs {F(a('risk', 'target_9478_weighted')['median'], 2)}%). The 220 eligible participants without complete pairs were less often non-Hispanic White ({F(a('nhw', 'noncompleters_220')['pct'])}% vs {F(a('nhw')['pct'])}%), had higher first-visit SBP and, among the {a('risk', 'noncompleters_220')['n']} with all first-visit inputs, higher median risk ({F(a('risk', 'noncompleters_220')['median'], 2)}%; post hoc).")
    h2('Study 1: primary outcome')
    v1c = [P(S13['by_visit1_category'][k]['estimate']) + '%' for k in '0123']
    p(f"Remeasurement changed the base PREVENT-ASCVD category in {pr['events']} of {pr['n']} participants ({cis(pr)}); the estimate was {pr['precision_label']}. Of these, {pr['up']} moved to a higher and {pr['down']} to a lower category, and {S5['non_adjacent']} moved by more than one category (Table 2 and Figure 2). Participants within 0.5 pp of a threshold made up {P(S5['window_0p5']['share_in_window'])}% of the sample but {P(S5['window_0p5']['share_of_changes_in_window'])}% of changes. Continuous agreement on the logit scale was high (ICC {S6['icc_a1']:.3f}; median absolute change in risk {F(S6['abs_dr_median_pp'], 2)} pp), and the 95% RCV of predicted risk was {P(rcv[0])}% to +{P(rcv[1])}% (Supplementary Table S9). A systematic shift between visits accounted for {S(100 * S9C['difference'])} pp of the {P(pr['estimate'])}% (95% CI {rng(*S9C['ci_corrected_bootstrap'])}; interval corrected for a coding error, Supplementary Tables S1 and S11). Post hoc, clustering on the visit-1 physician ({X2['E5']['n_examiners_v1']} physicians) widened the interval to {cin(X2['E5']['visit1_physician'])} (wild cluster bootstrap {P(X2['E5']['visit1_physician_wild_bootstrap']['lower'])}–{P(X2['E5']['visit1_physician_wild_bootstrap']['upper'])}%), wider than the 6 pp precision criterion (Supplementary Table S32).")
