    h2('Study 1: other thresholds and sensitivity analyses')
    oth = [R4['SA1a_exclude_out_of_domain']['theta']['estimate'], R4['SA2a_single_reading2']['theta']['estimate'], R4['SA3a_confirmed_diabetes_fixed']['theta']['estimate'], R4['SA5_referral_guard']['theta']['estimate'], R4['SA10_completeness_weighting']['theta_weighted']]
    pc, pu = (PH['calibrated_primary']['Psi_pp'], PH['uncalibrated_SA4a']['Psi_pp'])
    assert abs(pc['GLYC'] - pu['GLYC']) < 1e-09 and all((pu[g] > pc[g] for g in ['KIDNEY', 'BP', 'LIPID']))
    p(f"The 7.5% PREVENT 10-year total CVD threshold was crossed by {nof(S10['all_759'])} participants ({cis(S10['all_759'])}); in a post hoc curve, the chance of crossing 7.5% was at least 10% for first-visit total CVD risks of {F(CV['zones_risk_pct']['0.1'][0])}–{F(CV['zones_risk_pct']['0.1'][1])}% (Supplementary Table S28). Among the {S11['n']} participants aged 40–79 years, the PCE 7.5% threshold was crossed by {P(S11['cross75_sbp_only']['estimate'])}% when only SBP was remeasured, as in Ye and colleagues,[[ye2014]] and by {P(S11['cross75_full']['estimate'])}% when SBP, cholesterol and diabetes were remeasured (difference {cpi(S11['cross75_full_minus_sbp'])}; post hoc Tango interval {rng(*tg['tango95'])}; Supplementary Table S12), and the pipeline screen against Ye and colleagues passed (Supplementary Table S2). Among the prespecified key sensitivity analyses, only uncalibrated creatinine moved θ by at least 1.5 pp: {nof(sa4a)} ({cis(sa4a)}) changed category; post hoc, it lowered eGFR and raised the contributions of creatinine, blood pressure and lipids, with HbA1c unchanged (Supplementary Table S16). The other key analyses gave {P(min(oth))}–{P(max(oth))}%, and alternative interval methods gave similar intervals (Supplementary Table S15 and Figure S1).")
    h2('Study 2: urine specimen')
    sens = [v['estimate'] for v in S2['sensitivities'].values()]
    p(f"Of {fl2['age30_79']:,} participants aged 30–79 years in NHANES 2009–2010, {pa['n']:,} were eligible with both specimens (Supplementary Tables S17 and S18). Replacing random with first-morning UACR changed the category in {pa['events']} participants (weighted {cis(pa)}): {plo['events']} moved down and {phi['events']} up, all to an adjacent category (Table 2 and Figure 6A and 6B). Among {bp12['n']:,} participants with two eligible SBP readings, replacing reading 1 with reading 2 (post hoc benchmark) changed the category in {bp12['events']} ({cis(bp12)}), against {P(ur12['estimate'])}% ({cin(ur12)}) for the specimen change in the same participants (Supplementary Table S24). Sensitivity analyses gave {P(min(sens))}–{P(max(sens))}% and response weighting {P(rw['ipw_estimate'])}% (Supplementary Table S20). In the 2001–2002 sample, {ex['events']} of {ex['n']} changed category ({cis(ex)}); the interval exceeded the prespecified 6 pp width.")
    p(f"Post hoc, participants with both UACRs below 30 mg/g (weighted {P(fb['estimate'])}%) accounted for {cip(fbs)} of changes, with their own disagreement {P(fbd['estimate'])}%, and those within 0.5 pp of a threshold ({P(win['workload']['estimate'])}%) for {P(win['coverage']['estimate'])}% (Supplementary Tables S21–S23). Removing the average first-morning to random ratio ({X2['E8']['weighted_gmr_first_morning_over_random']:.2f}) left {cip(X2['E8']['shift_removed_any'])} changing, {P(X2['E8']['shift_removed_down']['estimate'])}% down and {P(X2['E8']['shift_removed_up']['estimate'])}% up (Supplementary Table S32).")
    h2('Post hoc analyses')
    ci = lambda k: f'{F(redci(k)[0], 0)}–{F(redci(k)[1], 0)}%'
    sh = x3['shapley']
    p(f"Among {x3['n_untreated_eligible']} untreated participants, the 2025 guideline's recommendation to start antihypertensive medication now applied to {P(x3['drug_now_v1']['estimate'])}% at visit 1 and {P(x3['drug_now_v2']['estimate'])}% at visit 2 and changed between visits for {x3['theta_rx']['events']} ({cis(x3['theta_rx'])}; Supplementary Table S31); {P(x3['p_not_rx2_given_rx1']['estimate'], 0)}% of those recommended medication at visit 1 were not at visit 2. Blood pressure accounted for {F(100 * sh['BP']['estimate'])} pp (95% CI {rng(sh['BP']['lower'], sh['BP']['upper'])}) of the {P(x3['theta_rx']['estimate'])}% and the other inputs for {F(100 * sh['nonBP']['estimate'])} pp; {x3['flips_with_stage_change']} of the {x3['theta_rx']['events']} changes involved a change in blood pressure stage, and {x3['flips_stage1_both_highrisk_change']} a change in the high-risk flag within stage 1 ({x3['flips_stage1_both_cvd75_only']} through the 7.5% criterion alone). The single-visit recommendation differed from that based on the mean of both visits for {P(x3['vs_two_visit_mean']['mean_single_visit_differs'])}% (95% CI {rng(x3['vs_two_visit_mean']['mean_single_visit_differs_ci']['lower'], x3['vs_two_visit_mean']['mean_single_visit_differs_ci']['upper'])}%), sensitivity analyses gave {P(min(x3sens))}–{P(max(x3sens))}%, and clustering on the visit-1 physician gave an interval of {cin(x3['theta_rx_visit1_physician'])} (Supplementary Table S31).")
    p(f"Under the measurement-error model (post hoc), {P(x4['primary']['kappa'])}% (95% CI {P(x4['ci']['kappa'][0])}–{P(x4['ci']['kappa'][1])}%) of single-visit base categories differed from the category of the usual level ({P(min(kap_all))}–{P(max(kap_all))}% across error distributions and deconvolution methods), against the test-retest disagreement of {P(pr['estimate'])}% (Supplementary Table S32). In model-based simulations, a second day of measurements for the {P(rs['t25_all']['repeat_workload'], 0)}% of simulated first assessments in the ≥25% zone reduced disagreement between two assessments by {red('t25_all'):.0f}% (95% interval {ci('t25_all')}), against {red('all2'):.0f}% if everyone had one (Supplementary Table S27 and Supplementary Figure S2).")
    eb, eu, s1c = (E1['base']['theta_lab'], E1['uacr']['theta_lab'], E1['study1_comparator'])
    p(f"In the 2001–2002 sample ({E1['flow']['all_second_exam_labs']} of {E1['flow']['study2_external']} with all second-examination laboratory values), remeasuring the laboratory inputs with blood pressure fixed changed the base category in {eb['events']} ({cis(eb)}), against {cip(s1c['base_lab_only_ref1'])} for the same contrast in Study 1, and, with urine also remeasured, the UACR-model category in {eu['events']} ({cis(eu)}), against {cip(s1c['uacr_lab_urine_ref1'])} (Figure 6C and Supplementary Table S29).")
    z25, s1h = (E2['zone_0.25'], E2['stage1_untreated'])
    mil = lambda x: f'{x:.0f}' if x >= 10 else f'{x:.1f}'
    p(f"In an exploratory transport to NHANES 2021–2023 (Supplementary Table S30), {P(z25['estimate'])}% (95% CI {cin(z25)}, survey sampling only; about {mil(z25['millions_scaled']['millions'])} million if missing inputs are unrelated to risk) of US adults aged 30–79 years without self-reported cardiovascular disease had a first-measurement risk inside the ≥25% instability zone, and {P(s1h['cvd_in_10pct_zone']['estimate'])}% of untreated adults whose blood pressure at one examination was in the stage 1 range had a total CVD risk of {F(CV['zones_risk_pct']['0.1'][0])}–{F(CV['zones_risk_pct']['0.1'][1])}%, where, under the transported curve, the chance of crossing 7.5% on remeasurement would be at least 10%.")
