def ref_text(key):
    if key in LOCAL:
        return LOCAL[key]
    hit = [r for r in REFV['references'] if r['key'] == key]
    if not hit:
        raise KeyError(f'reference {key} missing from reference_verification.json')
    r = hit[0]
    if r['status'] != 'verified':
        raise ValueError(f"reference {key} not verified: {r.get('notes', '')}")
    return r['citation']

def legends():
    return ['Figure 1. Study 1 flow (NHANES III); the Study 2 flow is in Supplementary Table S17. MEC, mobile examination center; MI, myocardial infarction; SBP, systolic blood pressure; TC, total cholesterol; HDL, HDL cholesterol; ACR, albumin-to-creatinine ratio; PCE, Pooled Cohort Equations. The reconstructed cohort was used only for the prespecified gross-error screen against Ye and colleagues;[[ye2014]] its step counts are compared with theirs (956 with three same-arm readings; 808 analysed).', 'Figure 2. Base and UACR-enhanced PREVENT 10-year ASCVD risk at the two visits. A and C, risk at visit 2 against visit 1 on log axes with the 3%, 5% and 10% thresholds; colored points changed category. B and D, counts of visit-1 by visit-2 category.', 'Figure 3. Contribution of each input group. A and B, symmetrized Shapley contributions to the proportion changing category, which sum to θ (A) or θ_U (B), with 95% cluster-bootstrap intervals (4,000 replicates). C, proportion changing category when only one group is remeasured (dark) and θ minus the proportion when that group is held fixed (light), both with visit 1 as reference; circles base model, squares UACR model; negative values indicate offsetting changes. Short dashed lines mark benchmarks on the relevant row: from other studies, which use different equations, categories and outcomes and are not directly comparable (Ye and colleagues, PCE, SBP remeasured, crossing 7.5%;[[ye2014]] Ogunwale and colleagues, PCE, within-visit reading swap;[[ogunwale2016]] Cole and colleagues, simulated lipid variation[[cole2023]]), and on the urine row from Study 2 (same UACR-enhanced equation and categories; random to first-morning urine in NHANES 2009–2010, survey-weighted). D, share of the mean squared change in the PREVENT linear predictor, with 95% bootstrap intervals.', 'Figure 4. Probability of a category change by distance from the nearest threshold. A and C condition on visit-1 risk (π_clin); B and D on the mean of both visits (π_mech). Curves are logistic regressions with a restricted cubic spline and nearest-threshold indicator; vertical bars are pointwise 95% cluster-bootstrap intervals at 0, 0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3 and 0.5 logit units; diamonds are observed proportions in distance bins (changes/n), with the open-ended >0.40 bin plotted at 0.55. Dotted line (B and D): probability that the absolute change in the linear predictor exceeds twice the distance. Horizontal lines at 10% and 25% define the instability zones; boxes in A and C give the corresponding first-visit risk ranges, truncated where another threshold becomes nearest.', 'Figure 5. Input variation and benchmarks. A, total within-person coefficient of variation (CVw), CVw net of analytical CV (model-based) across the analytical CV bracket, and published values from Lacher and colleagues[[lacher2005]] and the EFLM database[[eflm]] (no urine meta-analysis exists); creatinine is on the calibrated scale, with the uncalibrated-scale CVw shown as an open circle (post hoc), and the analytical CV was not rescaled to the calibrated scale. B, proportion changing base category under blood pressure scenarios with other inputs held at visit-1 values (95% CI); the bottom row is θ, with all inputs remeasured; reference lines are within-visit reading swaps in Study 2 (PREVENT-UACR, NHANES 2009–2010) and in ARIC.[[ogunwale2016]] C, model-based simulations: independent errors of the observed size (A) and analytical error only (B) at low and high analytical CV, beside the observed laboratory-only proportion and observed θ. D, SBP variance components expressed as SDs: between readings within a visit and between days.', f"Figure 6. Study 2 and sources of category change across both studies. A, PREVENT-UACR 10-year ASCVD risk with first-morning against random urine for {pa['n']:,} NHANES 2009–2010 participants (log axes; unweighted points) with the 3%, 5% and 10% thresholds; colored points changed category. B, counts of random-urine by first-morning-urine category (unweighted). C, proportion changing PREVENT-ASCVD category by source of measurement variation, with 95% CIs: circles, Study 1 (NHANES III; unweighted; cluster-robust intervals); squares, Study 2 (survey-weighted; Taylor-linearization intervals); triangles, NHANES 2001–2002 repeat sample (equal weights; cluster-adjusted intervals; the urine row exceeded the prespecified 6 pp width, and the laboratory rows are post hoc, with blood pressure not remeasured); open circles, single-group swaps from the Study 1 attribution analysis with visit 1 as reference (no interval). Study 1 rows use base PREVENT unless labelled PREVENT-UACR or UACR model; Study 2 rows and the 2001–2002 urine and laboratory + UACR rows use PREVENT-UACR, and the 2001–2002 laboratory row labelled base PREVENT uses the base equation. The Study 2 reading-swap row is a post hoc benchmark. The estimates differ in era, equation, weighting and sample and were not compared formally.", f"Figure 7. Repeat-measurement strategies in Study 1 (post hoc, model-based). Each input varies around the participant's visit mean with independent errors of the observed size (simulation model A); an assessment averages measurements over the stated number of days, and disagreement is the proportion of {pr['n']} participants whose base PREVENT-ASCVD category differs between two independent assessments made the same way (1,000 replicates per participant). A, simulated disagreement; the dashed line marks the observed θ. Open bars and symbols are targeted strategies, which take a second day of measurements only when the first estimate lies in the instability zone where π_clin is at least 25% or 10%. B, reduction in disagreement relative to one measurement against the mean number of additional measurement days per person, with 95% intervals from the 4,000 cluster-bootstrap replicates of participants (error SDs held fixed, so intervals understate uncertainty). The simulation assumes independent day-to-day errors of the 1988–1994 size and unchanged true values.", f"Central Illustration. Stability of PREVENT risk categories on remeasurement. Left, Study 1 (NHANES III; {pr['n']} adults; base PREVENT 10-year ASCVD equation; unweighted; cluster-robust 95% CI), with the symmetrized Shapley contributions of each input group, which sum to the proportion changing category (the HbA1c contribution reflects re-applying a single HbA1c ≥6.5% criterion at each visit), and Study 2 (NHANES 2009–2010; PREVENT with UACR; survey-weighted; Taylor-linearization 95% CI). Centre, modelled probability that a second standardized measurement of all routine inputs about 2 weeks later gives a different base category, by first-visit risk: the prespecified threshold-distance model (π_clin) shown on the risk scale (post hoc display, as in Table 3), with a pointwise 95% cluster-bootstrap band; the dips at {F(B35)}% and {F(B510)}% mark where the nearest threshold changes, and shading marks the zones where the probability is at least 25%. The probabilities apply to the Study 1 sample and include regression to the mean. Right, top: modelled probabilities far from a threshold (Table 3); bottom: post hoc decision analysis in the {x3['n_untreated_eligible']} untreated Study 1 participants (Supplementary Table S31): the proportion whose 2025 AHA/ACC guideline recommendation to start antihypertensive medication now (stage 2, or stage 1 with diabetes, chronic kidney disease or PREVENT 10-year total CVD risk ≥7.5%) differed between the two visits, with a CR1 95% CI, and its two-group Shapley split, and the number of changes that involved a change in blood pressure stage. ASCVD, atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease; UACR, urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio."]

def build(check=False):
    abs_ = abstract()
    kp = key_points()
    main = [('h1', 'Abstract')] + [('p', s) for s in abs_] + [('p', 'Keywords: cardiovascular risk; PREVENT equations; test-retest reliability; biological variation; blood pressure; albuminuria; NHANES')] + [('h1', 'Key Points')] + [('p', s) for s in kp] + body() + results() + discussion() + declarations()
    t1a, t1b = table1()
    tables = [('break',), ('table', t1a), ('break',), ('table', t1b), ('break',), ('table', table2()), ('break',), ('table', table4()), ('break',), ('table', table3())]
    figs = [('break',), ('h1', 'Figure legends')] + [('legend', s) for s in legends() if not s.startswith('Figure 7.')]
    OUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    from PIL import Image
    for i in list(range(1, 8)) + ['s1', 'ci']:
        Image.open(FIG / f'figure_{i}.png').convert('RGB').save(OUT / f'figure_{i}.png', dpi=(300, 300))
        shutil.copy2(FIG / f'figure_{i}.svg', OUT / f'figure_{i}.svg')
    figblocks = [('break',)] + sum([[('figure', OUT / f'figure_{i}.png', f'Figure {i}', 6.3), ('break',)] for i in range(1, 7)], []) + [('figure', OUT / 'figure_ci.png', 'Central Illustration', 6.5)]
    all_blocks = [('title', TITLE)] + main + tables + figs
    order = W.number_citations(all_blocks)
    stats = {'abstract_words': sum((len(re.sub('\\*\\*[^*]+\\*\\*', '', s).split()) for s in abs_)), 'main_text_words': W.words(body() + results() + discussion()), 'key_points_words': sum((len(re.sub('\\*\\*[^*]+\\*\\*', '', s).split()) for s in kp)), 'references': len(order), 'tables': 4, 'figures': 6, 'central_illustration': 1}
    print(json.dumps(stats))
    if check:
        Path(OUT).mkdir(exist_ok=True)
        txt = [W.render_cites(x[1], order) for x in [('title', TITLE)] + main if x[0] in ('p', 'h1', 'h2', 'title')]
        (OUT / 'draft_text_check.txt').write_text('\n\n'.join(txt) + '\n\nREFERENCE KEYS: ' + ', '.join(sorted(order, key=order.get)), encoding='utf-8')
        return stats
    refs = [ref_text(k) for k in sorted(order, key=order.get)]
    OUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    doc = W.new_doc(TITLE)
    W.render(doc, [('title', TITLE)], order)
    for s in ['Yunhao Jiang', 'The University of Edinburgh, Edinburgh, United Kingdom', 'Correspondence: Yunhao Jiang; biojiang777@gmail.com', f"Word count: abstract {stats['abstract_words']}; key points {stats['key_points_words']}; main text {stats['main_text_words']}. Tables 4; figures 6 and a central illustration; references {stats['references']}.", 'Short title: Measurement variation and PREVENT risk categories']:
        W.para(doc, s)
    W.page_break(doc)
    W.render(doc, main, order)
    W.para(doc, 'References', style='Heading 1')
    W.render(doc, [('refs', refs)], order)
    W.render(doc, tables + figs + figblocks, order)
    W.add_line_numbers(doc)
    out = OUT / 'nh3_testretest_manuscript.docx'
    doc.save(out)
    shutil.copy2(ST / 'analysis_protocol_v1.md', OUT / 'supplementary_protocol_v1.md')
    rec = {'revision': 6, 'condensed': 'Main text condensed from about 7,600 to under 5,000 words on 2026-10-10; Key Points and Central Illustration added; revision-4 Results text reproduced as Supplementary Results; revision-4 docx and builders archived in manuscript/extended_rev4/', 'merge': 'Urine-specimen manuscript (studies/uacr_prevent) merged as Study 2 on 2026-10-09; values read from manuscript_evidence_v1/study2_evidence.json without reanalysis', 'review_applied': ['wf_47ea3196-9ae (85 confirmed findings; manuscript/review_round1_response.json)', 'wf_d7bb43be-c55 fix verification (75 of 85 resolved after revision 2; remaining 10 and 10 new minor/major items, including the S9 interval coding error, addressed in revision 3)', 'wf_46b5c4b7-031 merge review (28 confirmed, partly overlapping; 4 refuted; manuscript/review_merge_response.json)', 'wf_70e4f249-73d additions review (manuscript/review_additions_response.json)', 'revision 5 condensation review: fidelity, protocol and editor reviewers, two verification rounds (manuscript/review_condense_response.json)'], 'built_from': {str(p.relative_to(ROOT)): hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in [A1 / 'stage3/stage3_results.json', A1 / 'stage4/stage4_results.json', A1 / 'deviation_log.json', EV / 'table1.json', EV / 'reference_verification.json', ST / 'analysis_v1_posthoc/sa4a_decomposition.json', ST / 'analysis_v1_posthoc/review_round1.json', ST / 'analysis_v1_corrections/s9_and_swap_counts.json', ST / 'analysis_protocol_v1.md', EV / 'study2_evidence.json', ST / 'analysis_v1_posthoc/reclassification_lookup.json', ST / 'analysis_v1_posthoc/repeat_strategies.json', ST / 'analysis_v1_posthoc/cvd75_curve.json', ST / 'analysis_v1_posthoc/ext2001_labs.json', ST / 'analysis_v1_posthoc/ext2021_burden.json', ST / 'extensions_protocol_20261010.md', ST / 'analysis_v1_posthoc/ext2_results.json', ST / 'extensions2_protocol_20261010.md']}, 'revision6': '2026-10-10: second post hoc set (extensions2_protocol_20261010.md, saved before E3): E3 2025 BP-guideline drug-initiation decision (main text, abstract, Key Points, Central Illustration), E4 model-based disagreement with the usual-level category, E5 physician clustering, E6 BP minus lipid, E7 heteroscedastic standardization, E8 Study 2 shift; repeat-strategy simulation moved from main Figure 7 to Supplementary Figure S2; Bene-Alhasan 2026 and Rahimi 2025 added; reviewed by fidelity and code/protocol auditors (manuscript/review_rev6_response.json)', 'stats': stats, 'reference_order': sorted(order, key=order.get), 'protocol_rules': {'abstract_flagged_key_SA': flagged, 'headline_rule_base_curve_first': K4['headline_rule_curve_first'], 'headline_rule_uacr_curve_first': K4U['headline_rule_curve_first'], 'uacr_handling': 'abstract summarizes the UACR model per protocol by its curve (threshold values); Results give the 10% zones', 'delta_U_wording': wording(dlu), 'attribution_statement': f"BP largest (rank-first {K2['Psi']['BP']['rank_first_freq']:.4f} >= 0.90)", 'interpretive_a': K2['interpretive_a'], 'interpretive_b': S12['interpretive_b'], 'interpretive_c_flag': S8['base']['interpretive_c_flag'], 'interpretive_d': R4['SA5_referral_guard']['interpretive_d_treatment_feedback'], 'interpretive_e_abstract_both': R4['SA3a_confirmed_diabetes_fixed']['interpretive_e_abstract_both'], 'interpretive_f': R4['SA14a_exclude_albumin_bdl']['interpretive_f_sensitive'], 'e14': 'supplement only (Table S14)', 'zones': 'truncated at logit midpoints between thresholds'}, 'author_actions': ['Choose target journal and adapt format/word limits', 'Decide on public release of code/derived data (GitHub/Zenodo) and add the link', 'Decide whether to register/timestamp the protocol hash publicly', 'Add degree/ORCID if required', 'Add any journal-required statement on use of AI tools (left to the author)', 'Run the dated novelty search again immediately before submission', 'Main text is under 5,000 words (revision 5); the revision-4 extended version is archived in manuscript/extended_rev4/ for venues without a word limit', 'Supplementary tables follow the protocol reporting order and are first cited out of numerical order in the main text; renumber only if the venue requires it']}
    (OUT / 'build_record.json').write_text(json.dumps(rec, indent=1) + '\n', encoding='utf-8')
    print('saved', out)
if __name__ == '__main__':
    build(check='--check' in sys.argv)
